==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]].
*1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 98% HP:
**1 [[Nimoy Bore]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 97% HP:
**1 [[Razorback]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 96% HP:
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
Realistically, the only thing you need to do is lure every single boss, kill it, and trigger the next boss with a low damage per hit unit. Do not use any cats with above 30,000 HP or with Survive during the first 4 bosses. The best way to do this is to use a small-damage unit like [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]] to spawn one boss at a time, and also dying to the wave from the base.

As for each individual boss, it is recommended to use crowd control to subdue and destroy them one at a time. Recommended units to do so are [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] for the Bore, [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]] for the Nimoy Bore, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bomber]] for the Razorback and Kurosawah, and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] or [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet]] for Boraphim.

==Trivia==
*This stage is almost certainly a reference to the [[Wikipedia:Bay of Pigs Invasion|Bay of Pigs Invasion]] in April 1961, which involved a US-funded Cuban paramilitary force attempting to land on a beachhead in Cuba with the goal of ousting the revolutionary government headed by Fidel Castro. While landing did succeed, the entire group was defeated and imprisoned just three days later.

